From 04350e2813cd050013812cd3d4b2eded3f3f9333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Minh Ha-Duong <minh.haduong@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 08:59:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(search): refuse mode:"semantic" when nothing can
 embed the query, not just when vectors are missing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Semantic ranking needs both ends of the comparison — vectors in the index, and
an embedder to turn the query into one — but the refusal only tested the first.
An index built with an embedder and reopened with ZOTEUS_EMBEDDINGS=off keeps
its vectors: reconcileVectorProvenance has no current identity to compare them
against, so they are unusable rather than known-wrong and stay on the rows. That
makes hasVectors true, so the 0-vector refusal never fires; query() then closes
the keyword ranker (mode !== 'semantic' is false) and never builds a query
vector (opts.embedder is undefined), and returns []. The tool renders that as a
bare `No matches for "…"`, which is exactly the #7 failure mode the refusal
exists to prevent — an empty page indistinguishable from a library that holds
nothing on the subject. Nothing else covers it either: embedderNotice is
deliberately silent when embeddings were switched off on purpose, so the one
sentence that would have explained the empty page is suppressed by design.

The gate now tests hasVectors AND hasEmbedder, and the message names which half
is missing. The 0-vector wording is unchanged; the new branch says how many
vectors are stranded and either points at ZOTEUS_EMBEDDINGS or names the
configured provider and why it is not running. It is the same refusal an index
with no vectors and a downed embedder already got, which differed only in
whether the index happened to hold rows the query could not reach.

Unaffected: "auto" and "keyword", which do not need the query embedded, and a
provider that fails during the query itself — embedderActive is still true when
the gate runs, and the existing post-query notice reports it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JjUPSUzz4wLjNTNPLSLzir
